WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:05.792
- Los Angeles is home.

00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:09.311
I was born and raised here.

00:00:09.311 --> 00:00:11.041
I come from midwives

00:00:11.041 --> 00:00:15.041
and I heard their stories
as a child growing up.

00:00:16.443 --> 00:00:19.076
In Los Angeles County
African American women

00:00:19.076 --> 00:00:22.081
are two to three times
more likely to suffer

00:00:22.081 --> 00:00:26.248
premature birth or to have a
baby die within the first year.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.256
You have to ask the question:

00:00:30.256 --> 00:00:32.396
is the hospital really
the safest place for them?

00:00:32.396 --> 00:00:36.156
And my mission is all
around making a change in

00:00:36.156 --> 00:00:37.515
these statistics.

00:00:37.515 --> 00:00:39.932
(soft music)

00:00:42.715 --> 00:00:43.798
Oh, it's okay!

00:00:45.479 --> 00:00:47.257
Midwifery is closing the gap

00:00:47.257 --> 00:00:50.257
because each person is given a path.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.780
Midwives are not anti-hospitals,

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.727
midwives are not anti-doctors.

00:00:55.727 --> 00:00:58.620
We are advocates for people having access

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.019
to the care that they want.

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:02.202
That means they have
the choice to give birth

00:01:02.202 --> 00:01:04.180
in a hospital, in a birth center

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.947
or at home but supporting
them whichever way they go

00:01:06.947 --> 00:01:10.086
and then them getting
the best possible care.

00:01:10.086 --> 00:01:12.528
Right now if you were to
Google midwifery you would find

00:01:12.528 --> 00:01:16.268
the majority of people
represented are an elite group.

00:01:16.268 --> 00:01:20.385
More specifically, white
and so I see myself

00:01:20.385 --> 00:01:23.630
as hopefully someone who's
an advocate for those

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.029
that are completely
disregarded and unseen in

00:01:26.029 --> 00:01:27.112
our community

00:01:27.982 --> 00:01:29.306
and if you ask those women,

00:01:29.306 --> 00:01:30.378
they'll tell you.

00:01:30.378 --> 00:01:32.102
Well, it feels really good
to be seen by someone

00:01:32.102 --> 00:01:35.434
who looks like me, who
understands the micro-aggression,

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:38.857
who understands the stress of
just being a person of color

00:01:38.857 --> 00:01:40.259
in the United States.

00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:41.659
This is the Community Birth Center

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:43.508
and it's located in mid-city.

00:01:43.508 --> 00:01:45.425
I run the birth center.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.383
It was funded by women in the community

00:01:48.383 --> 00:01:51.438
who I had served as a midwife.

00:01:51.438 --> 00:01:52.677
What they find when they come

00:01:52.677 --> 00:01:54.282
is a warm, inviting space.

00:01:54.282 --> 00:01:55.728
When they make it into the exam room,

00:01:55.728 --> 00:01:57.000
it's a conversation.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.352
What's going on, what
can I do for you today?

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:00.379
You're fine.

00:02:00.379 --> 00:02:02.153
- When I get to nine months
I'm gonna have like a

00:02:02.153 --> 00:02:03.515
small planet attached to the front of me.

00:02:03.515 --> 00:02:04.509
- You're great.

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:08.390
Last year, 2014, I had one premature baby

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:11.751
out of 100 babies born
outside of the hospital

00:02:11.751 --> 00:02:13.279
and in the hospital.

00:02:13.279 --> 00:02:15.213
One premature baby.

00:02:15.213 --> 00:02:17.380
That's kind of a big deal.

00:02:19.045 --> 00:02:20.612
Are you having any dizziness

00:02:20.612 --> 00:02:22.130
or any light-headedness?

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:25.262
Most midwives in a day are
gonna see six to 10 people,

00:02:25.262 --> 00:02:27.370
maybe on a really busy day 20.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.921
As opposed to having to have
the caseload of a doctor.

00:02:30.921 --> 00:02:32.407
This is where we see a big difference

00:02:32.407 --> 00:02:34.675
specifically for African
American families.

00:02:34.675 --> 00:02:37.092
(soft music)

00:02:38.672 --> 00:02:40.401
The Community Birth Center
offers a sliding scale

00:02:40.401 --> 00:02:42.218
for families in need.

00:02:42.218 --> 00:02:45.309
The average cost for out-of-
hospital birth with a midwife

00:02:45.309 --> 00:02:48.141
in Los Angeles is 6,500 dollars.

00:02:48.141 --> 00:02:49.959
I charge $5,000.

00:02:49.959 --> 00:02:51.323
I could never charge someone something

00:02:51.323 --> 00:02:53.240
that I couldn't afford.

00:02:56.955 --> 00:02:58.938
Being a single mom,

00:02:58.938 --> 00:03:02.660
there are days that I don't
feel like I have enough:

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:05.750
fiscally, emotionally, spiritually,

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.529
all of them; I just don't have enough

00:03:08.529 --> 00:03:10.196
but I figure it out.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.188
Will lack of income ultimately close

00:03:14.188 --> 00:03:15.559
the Community Birth Center?

00:03:15.559 --> 00:03:17.414
It's a very strong possibility

00:03:17.414 --> 00:03:20.176
but I'll keep doing it
for as long as I can

00:03:20.176 --> 00:03:23.593
and I will never stop giving people care.

00:03:25.688 --> 00:03:29.030
I will never stop the sliding scale.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:31.005
It comes with great sacrifice

00:03:31.005 --> 00:03:33.231
but it's worth it.

00:03:33.231 --> 00:03:35.648
(soft music)

